  What's missing: src/AtmScatter/CRTM_AerosolScatter.f90

  Nothing ever writes to AScat%Absorption_Optical_Depth. This is the core of the
  job. In CRTM's terms (ke is the extinction coefficient, w is the single
  scattering albedo, c is the layer concentration), each part needs the
  following:

  - Forward (CRTM_Compute_AerosolScatter, near line 287, next to the
    Optical_Depth sum):
  AScat%Absorption_Optical_Depth(ka) = AScat%Absorption_Optical_Depth(ka) + &
       (ONE - ASV%w(ka,n)) * ASV%ke(ka,n) * Atm%Aerosol(n)%Concentration(ka)
    This has to sit outside the IF (n_Phase_Elements > 0 .and. 
    Include_Scattering) block. AAOD needs w, but it must not depend on the
    scattering switch.
  - TL (near line 509):
    aaod_TL += (1-w)*(ke*c_TL + ke_TL*c) - w_TL*ke*c
  - AD (near line 739): transpose the TL line, adding to c_AD, ke_AD and a new
    w_AD term. Right now w_AD only gets contributions through bs_AD, and only
    when scattering is on.

  Watch-out: the clipping of w. The forward code forces w into [0,1] at lines
  262–273, and sets w=0 whenever ke<=0. Wherever that clipping kicks in, w_TL
  and w_AD must be zero. Otherwise the TL/AD consistency test will fail.

  Units. Your formula uses qm, a mixing ratio. Inside CRTM the variable is
  Aerosol%Concentration in kg/m² per layer. The conversion from mixing ratio
  happens upstream in UFO, so CRTM only needs the extinction coefficient and SSA
  from the lookup table, both of which it already has.

  Suggested order

  1. Forward: add the AAOD sum in CRTM_Compute_AerosolScatter, then check it
     against a hand calculation (/crtm_aaod_forward).
  2. TL and AD: in CRTM_AerosolScatter.f90, taking care with the w clipping
     (/crtm_aaod_tlad).
  3. Tests: write the missing test_AAOD.f90 programs for forward, TL, AD and
     K-matrix, then build and run the TL/AD checks (/crtm_aaod_create_tests).

  Should I start with the forward change?

