● I added an optional AAOD flag to all four functions in
  src/AtmScatter/CRTM_AOD_Module.f90: CRTM_AOD, CRTM_AOD_TL, CRTM_AOD_AD and
  CRTM_AOD_K. The file compiles cleanly on its own, but I couldn't build the
  full library or run any tests (explained below).

  How it works
  - Argument: it's a new last argument, LOGICAL, OPTIONAL, INTENT(IN) :: AAOD.
    Inside each function a local Compute_AAOD defaults to .FALSE. and takes the
    flag's value when you pass it.
  - Forward and TL: with the flag on, Layer_Absorption_Optical_Depth (and its TL
    counterpart) is copied from AtmOptics. With it off, the field is set to
    zero.
  - AD and K: the AAOD adjoint input from RTSolution_AD or RTSolution_K is
    passed into the calculation only when the flag is on. Otherwise it is
    ignored.
  - Docs: each function's header comments now describe the flag and show it in
    the calling sequence.

  With the flag off or left out, the functions give exactly the results they
  gave before, so existing callers such as UFO don't need changes. To turn it
  on, call for example CRTM_AOD_TL(..., Options=opts, AAOD=.TRUE.).

  Build status
  - Compile check: the file compiles with the build's own compiler (mpiifort)
    and -warn all, with no errors or warnings. I built it against the module
    files already in your build directory and wrote the output to my scratchpad,
    so nothing in the build tree was touched.
