● I've carried the AAOD flag into AtmOptics, so CRTM_Compute_AerosolScatter and
  its TL and AD now compute AAOD when you pass AAOD=.TRUE.. All three changed
  files compile with no errors or warnings. I haven't yet run any numerical
  check (forward values, TL against finite differences, or the adjoint
  dot-product test), because the full library still can't be rebuilt.

  Changes
  1. AtmOptics/CRTM_AtmOptics_Define.f90: new field LOGICAL :: Include_AAOD = 
     .FALSE., next to Include_Scattering. It is also included when two AtmOptics
     structures are compared.
  2. AtmScatter/CRTM_AOD_Module.f90: each function sets Include_AAOD = 
     Compute_AAOD on its AtmOptics structures (AtmOptics and its _TL, _AD or _K
     partner) at every channel. When the flag is off, CRTM_AerosolScatter.f90
     now skips the AAOD calculation entirely.
  3. AtmScatter/CRTM_AerosolScatter.f90: the calculation, in terms of extinction
     coefficient ke, single scattering albedo w and layer concentration c. It
     runs only when Include_AAOD is on:

  ┌─────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┐
  │         │  Scattering on (the normal AOD case)  │    Scattering off     │
  ├─────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┤
  │ Forward │ aaod += (1-w)·ke·c                    │ aaod += ke·c          │
  ├─────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┤
  │ TL      │ (1-w)(ke_TL·c + ke·c_TL) − w_TL·ke·c  │ ke_TL·c + ke·c_TL     │
  ├─────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┤
  │ AD      │ c_AD += (1-w)·ke·aaod_AD, ke_AD +=    │ c_AD += ke·aaod_AD,   │
  │         │ (1-w)·c·aaod_AD, w_AD −= ke·c·aaod_AD │ ke_AD += c·aaod_AD    │
  └─────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────┘

  Why the two columns: when scattering is off, Get_Aerosol_Opt has already
  replaced ke with ke·(1-w), so ASV%ke is the absorption coefficient. Applying
  (1-w) again would count it twice. The TL and AD lookup routines follow the
  same convention, so the dependence on w is still carried through correctly in
  that case.

  Clipping of w and ke: in the AD, the new terms go before the existing clipping
  step, which zeroes w_AD and ke_AD where the forward code clipped w to [0,1]
  or zeroed ke. In the TL they come after the matching clipping. So the clipping
  treats AAOD the same way it treats AOD.

  Still to do
  - Full rebuild needed: adding a field to CRTM_AtmOptics_type changes that
    structure, so everything that uses it (CRTM, then UFO) must be recompiled.
  - CMake is still blocked: test/CMakeLists.txt registers AAOD tests whose
    test_AAOD.f90 main programs don't exist yet. Until they're written, make in
    the jedi-bundle build fails at the configure step.
  - Suggested next step: /crtm_aaod_create_tests. It would write those main
    programs and run the TL/AD checks with AAOD=.TRUE., and I can also check the
    forward AAOD against a hand calculation from the lookup-table ke and w.

  Something I noticed but didn't touch: in the existing TL code, when scattering
  is on, Backscat_Coefficient gets its TL contribution added twice, and the AD
  adds it only once. If a TL/AD test checks backscatter, it may fail for that
  reason, which has nothing to do with AAOD.

