  test_Unit_AerosolScatter_AAOD_TL (test_AerosolScatter_AAOD_TL.f90)
  - Flag off: with Include_AAOD off, AAOD is exactly zero and AOD is bit-for-bit
    unchanged.
  - Forward value: forward AAOD equals Σ(1-w)·ke·ρ computed from the table
    values, and AAOD ≤ AOD.
  - Scattering on/off: AAOD is the same either way, and with scattering off AAOD
    = AOD. This confirms the (1-w) factor isn't applied twice.
  - TL vs finite difference: TL matches a central finite difference, with
    relative error about 1e-11 for concentration and 1e-9 for RH, with
    scattering on and off.

  test_Unit_AerosolScatter_AAOD_AD (test_AerosolScatter_AAOD_AD.f90)
  - Dot-product test: checks that the AD is the exact transpose of the TL. It
    passes to about 1e-15 with scattering on and off.
    - It runs once with only the AAOD adjoint input set.
    - It runs again with AAOD, AOD, SSA, asymmetry factor and phase coefficients
      all set together.
  - Flag off: with the flag off, an AAOD adjoint input has no effect.

  test_Unit_AerosolScatter_AAOD_K (test_AerosolScatter_AAOD_K.f90), which calls
  CRTM_AOD, CRTM_AOD_TL and CRTM_AOD_K directly with the AAOD= flag:
  - Flag off: AAOD=.FALSE. gives zero AAOD and unchanged AOD.
  - Jacobians vs TL: every column-AAOD Jacobian element (16 channels × 5 layers
    × 19 aerosols for concentration, plus RH) matches the TL. The largest
    difference is 7.6e-15 on values up to about 1e3.
  - Linearity: column AAOD = Σ ρ·∂AAOD/∂ρ, as it should since AAOD is linear in
    concentration. Relative difference is 2e-16.
  - Flag off in K: AAOD=.FALSE. ignores the AAOD adjoint input.

