● There's only one structure involved. AtmOptics, AScat and AerosolScatter are
  three local names for the same object, which has type CRTM_AtmOptics_type:

  - In CRTM_AOD_Module.f90, the variable is declared as
    TYPE(CRTM_AtmOptics_type) :: AtmOptics (lines 165, 471 and 809).
  - In CRTM_Compute_AerosolScatter / _TL / _AD, AtmOptics arrives as the
    argument AScat (or AScat_TL, AScat_AD), also declared
    TYPE(CRTM_AtmOptics_type) (lines 181, 425–429 and 645–646).
  - Get_Aerosol_Opt receives the same structure again and calls it
    AerosolScatter. That's where AerosolScatter%Include_Scattering is read and
    ke = ke*(1-w) is applied.

  So setting AtmOptics%Include_Scattering = .FALSE. in the AOD module is exactly
  what Get_Aerosol_Opt later sees as AerosolScatter%Include_Scattering. The
  module doesn't declare a separate "AerosolScatter" variable, so AtmOptics is
  the name there to set.

  About AtmScatter: CRTM_AtmScatter_type in
  AtmScatter/CRTM_AtmScatter_Define.f90 is an older structure. The current
  forward, TL, AD, K and AOD code doesn't use it. It's only referenced by legacy
  or auxiliary code (UWisc SOI, ODCAPS, the statistics tools, and the AtmOptics
  test programs). The AtmScatter/ directory name is left over from that design,
  but the aerosol routines in it now work on CRTM_AtmOptics_type.

